<!--
  NEGATIVE FIXTURE. Do not "fix" the missing BToA0Tag below.

  Clause 8.7.1.5 requires a Display HDR ColorSpace Profile to carry the BToA0Tag beside
  its mandatory AToB0Tag, and requires the pair whenever an AToBxTag is present.
  (8.7.1.3 c) says the same without the class condition, but 8.7.1.3 is
  informative, so 8.7.1.5 governs - PROPOSAL-ISSUE HDR-09.) This profile has an
  AToB0Tag and no BToA0Tag.

  The general validator reports it too, and more severely. The Display branch
  of CIccProfile::CheckRequiredTags() accepts the AToB0/BToA0 pair OR the six
  matrix column and TRC tags; with the pair incomplete it falls back to
  requiring the TRC tags, which an HDR ColorSpace Profile may not carry, so this profile is
  a critical error there ("Critical tag(s) missing"). The HDR rules add what
  that message cannot say: which clause 8.7.1 requirement is broken.

  Expected: iccFromXml saves the profile, and iccDumpProfile -v reports
    "HDR: BToA0Tag missing" and
    "HDR: AToB0Tag present without its paired BToA0Tag"
  See Testing/expected-invalid-fromxml.tsv.
-->
